  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Risk-based Approaches to Border Security in Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project aims to support Sri Lanka Customs to improve screening of passenger goods and courier packages in line with the Custom Ordinance through technological assessment and procurement of priority equipment; technical assistance on application of risk assessment principles and improvement to Customs intra-agency coordination; related training for relevant Customs divisions; process improvements to the data schema utilized by the Sri Lanka Border Risk Assessment Center (BRAC) for passenger risk assessment; and Technical assistance on relevant legal frameworks to support institutionalization of risk-management authorities and processes.</narrative>
  </description>
